  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PNG State and Resilience Building Contract (SRBC)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The action addresses some of the critical challenges of sustainable and inclusive development in PNG (climate change, access to safe water, violence). It will contribute to the Global Gateway investment priorities &#xbf;Climate and energy&#xbf; and &#xbf;Health&#xbf; by strengthening macroeconomics stability and easier access to justice. It will contribute to the general principle of creating a more viable environment for the investments at national level. The action will support the PNG&#xbf;s Medium Term Development Plan IV 2023-2027 (MTDP IV) and indirectly the targeted sector policies identified in the plan as important to promote inclusive growth and transformation in the country (Enhanced Nationally Determined Contribution 2020; National WaSH Policy 2015-2030; Crime Prevention through the revitalized Village Courts System Strategy 2020-2030). This intervention&amp;nbsp;will be implemented as State and Resilience Building Budget Support Programme. This Action contributes to the objectives of the EU Strategy for Cooperation in the Indo-Pacific and the implementation of the Green transition component of the Global Gateway Strategy as well as the Paris Agreement, and several components of the EU Green Deal. It will focus on SDGs 1, 3, 5, 6, 13 and 16. Building on the experience of the 11th EDF EU-PNG Partnership for Good Governance Budget Support, it will be a State and Resilience Building Budget Support Programme focusing on the three Priority Areas (PA) of the MIP: -PA1- Forestry-Climate Change-Biodiversity nexus, in particular SO 1 (An enabling evidence-based legal, regulatory and institutional framework for FCCB is in place, including through improved stakeholder participation and improved institutional coordination.)-PA2 -&#xbf;Water is Life&#xbf; Water, sanitation and hygiene (WaSH) in connection with Human Development for&amp;nbsp;SO 2 (WaSH policy makers and implementers operate effectively in an enabling environment with adequate capacities (including digital) towards the achievement of national WaSH goals.)-PA3- Transparent and accountable Governance, in particular SO 2 (Increased equitable access to and use of essential human rights protection services and peace building/ conflict prevention processes).The Overall Objective (Impact) of the action is to contribute to PNG&#xbf;s national growth, transformation and prosperity. The indicative Specific Objectives (SO) (subject to confirmation during formulation phase) are:&lt;span style=&quot;col</narrative>
  </description>
